    "v1.4-lite resolves required_anchors using markdown KB sources only (fast). PDFs remain referenced via SEARCH hints until explicit page anchors are added.",
    "v1.5-min adds PDF page-precise anchors for ProdFA_STRICT and ProcFA_STRICT using TRIZ_Corpus pages (1123-1125,1175,359,361,371). Other tools remain nonpdf-anchored pending mapping.",
    "v1.6-compendium adds PDF page anchors for remaining tools using Extensions Compendium/Rubina/ARIZ PDFs (limited page scan). Tools not found remain nonpdf.",
    "v1.7-step resolves CECA/Diversion/Robustness via stepped scan of Extensions Compendium to avoid timeouts.",
    "v1.8-force attempts stepped scans on TRIZ_Corpus and Addendum to resolve CECA/Diversion/Robustness page anchors.",
    "v1.9-diversion-nocorpus attempts to resolve diversion using compendium/addendum only (no corpus scan to avoid timeouts).",
    "v2.1 resolves DIVERSION_ANALYSIS by searching for 'Smart Saboteur' keyword in Compendium/Addendum.",
    "v2.2 sets DIVERSION_ANALYSIS PDF anchors using Russian 'Диверсионный анализ' section in MetaLens_v28.1.0_Addendum.pdf (pp.59,61,63,65).",
    "v2.3 adds bilingual alias fields (aliases_en/aliases_ru/acronyms_ru/acronym_guards) and a global RU glossary + guarded acronym rules.",
    "MINPATCH_v1: ancillary policy/contract/linter/schema/stubs embedded to reduce KB file count; external files removed from patchset.",
    "v4_8k_20: removed dangling references to non-packed markdown files; restored TRIZ PDF-anchor preference marker; embedded TESE_QUICK_INDEX for fast TESE_CARD/TESE_PATH use.",
    "v30.0.12: added Feygenson mature-system KB support (growth vs development, micro-trends, new areas/reverse-FOS, functional synthesis) without new visible tool."
